---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'August 9, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — Trustbread" showNav={false}>
  <div class="fade-in">
    <div class="page-head">
      <a href="/profil/" class="page-back">←</a>
      <div class="page-title">Privacy Policy</div>
      <p class="page-sub">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>

    <article class="policy">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>Trustbread</strong> (“we”, “us”, or “our”)
        handles information when you use the Trustbread mobile application and related website
        (the “App”).
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Trustbread is a sourdough baking companion that provides recipes, guides, blog articles,
        and product information. Contact for privacy questions:
        <a href="mailto:privacy@trustbread.app">privacy@trustbread.app</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you use the App, we may process:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Usage data</strong> — basic technical information such as device type, operating
          system version, and general App interaction needed to keep the App running.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Local preferences</strong> — settings stored only on your device (for example
          language or display preferences, when those features are enabled).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Information you choose to provide</strong> — for example if you contact support
          by email, we receive the content of that message and your email address.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The App does <strong>not</strong> require creating an account to browse recipes, guides,
        or blog content. We do not sell your personal data.
      </p>

      <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
      <p>We use information only to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide and improve App features and content</li>
        <li>Maintain security and diagnose technical issues</li>
        <li>Respond to support requests</li>
        <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        The App may contain links to external sites or stores (for example Amazon product pages).
        Those services have their own privacy policies. We are not responsible for their practices.
      </p>
      <p>
        If the App is distributed through Google Play or the Apple App Store, those platforms may
        collect analytics or crash data according to their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Data storage and retention</h2>
      <p>
        Local preferences remain on your device until you clear App data or uninstall the App.
        Support emails are kept only as long as needed to resolve your request, unless a longer
        period is required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Children’s privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The App is not directed at children under 13 (or the minimum age required in your country).
        We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has
        provided personal data, contact us and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live (for example the EEA, UK, or California), you may have rights
        to access, correct, delete, or restrict processing of your personal data, and to lodge a
        complaint with a supervisory authority. To exercise these rights, email
        <a href="mailto:privacy@trustbread.app">privacy@trustbread.app</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top
        will change when we do. Continued use of the App after changes means you accept the
        updated policy.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Trustbread — Privacy<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@trustbread.app">privacy@trustbread.app</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    padding: 0 var(--page-pad-x) 40px;
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .policy p,
  .policy li {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .policy h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 22px;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 28px 0 10px;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .policy ul {
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .policy li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .policy a {
    color: var(--tb-burgundy);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .policy strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
